# Augentic Plugins - Specify Specialist Skills

This repository provides specialist skills and references for Specify-driven development on Augentic's Omnia runtime and Crux cross-platform framework.

## Vocabulary

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#vocabulary).

## Operating Model

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#workflow-overview). Specify owns the workflow contract; this repository contributes specialist analysis, generation, enrichment, and review behavior on top of that contract.

Workflow skills orchestrate phases; **engineering standards** live in rules (`codex/rules/` and per-adapter `prose/rules/` overlays); **authoring standards** live in [`docs/standards/`](../../docs/standards/). See [standards layer](../../docs/explanation/standards-layer.md).

## Main Inputs

1. **TypeScript → Rust WASM**: reconstruct baseline specs and design from an existing service.
2. **Manual → Crux App**: generate cross-platform Crux applications (Rust core, iOS shell, Android shell, design system).

## Authority Hierarchy

When conflicts arise, follow this strict precedence order:

1. **SKILL.md** - generation rules and hard constraints
2. **Specify artifacts** - `proposal.md`, `spec.md`, `design.md`, `tasks.md` (Vectis also: `tokens.yaml`, `assets.yaml`; `composition.yaml` is a target build output, not a Specify artifact)
3. **docs/reference/**, **docs/standards/** (authoring house style — not engineering standards), and **sources/`<name>`/prose/prompts/** / **targets/`<name>`/prose/prompts/** in specify-adapters (+ each adapter's local `references/`) - authoritative patterns and examples
4. **Evidence** - source-extracted material; reference for ambiguity only
5. **LLM inference** - only after explicit evidence; prefer `[unknown]`

For `spec.md` requirement disagreements (the closed `authority` enum and its resolution order), see [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#authority-and-reconciliation-mechanics) and [synthesis/authority.md](../../plugins/spec/references/synthesis/authority.md); for the adapter contract, see [docs/explanation/adapter-anatomy.md](../../docs/explanation/adapter-anatomy.md).

**Key principle**: If artifacts conflict with source, trust the artifacts. If artifacts are incomplete, mark unknowns rather than guessing.

## Artifact Boundaries

See [docs/explanation/artifacts.md](../../docs/explanation/artifacts.md) for the per-artifact responsibility breakdown and [docs/explanation/augentic-specify-usage.md](../../docs/explanation/augentic-specify-usage.md) for the specialist-vs-artifact dividing line (behavioral specs stay platform-neutral; target-specific detail lives in specialist skills and references, not `spec.md`).

## Specialist Skills

See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#skill--cli-responsibility-split) for the skill / CLI responsibility split. Per-skill detail (description, argument hints, body) lives in each plugin's `SKILL.md` frontmatter under `plugins/<plugin>/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`.

## Repository Layout

See [docs/reference/directory-layout.md](../../docs/reference/directory-layout.md) for the full directory structure. Key directories:

```text
/.cursor/rules/           # Project guidance for agents
/.cursor-plugin/          # Multi-plugin marketplace manifest
/docs/                    # Extended documentation (explanation, contributing)
/plugins/
  ├── spec/               # Specify workflow plugin (init, plan, refine, build, merge, finalize, drop) + shared references/
  ├── capture/            # Runtime capture plugin (wiretap / migration capture)
  └── client/             # Client-facing deliverables (SoW, proposals, pricing)
/tests/framework_quality/ # Prose/manifest framework checks as cargo tests
/scripts/                 # Validation and plugin management
```

Shared codex rule packs (`codex/rules/universal/`, the `UNI-*` engineering rules) live in [`augentic/specify-adapters`](https://github.com/augentic/specify-adapters) alongside the adapter trees.

Source and target adapter trees (guest crates + `prose/prompts/`, per-adapter `prose/rules/` overlays, and the `codex/references/` prose embedded into components) live in [`augentic/specify-adapters`](https://github.com/augentic/specify-adapters).

## Validation

```bash
cargo test --test framework_quality   # the prose/manifest framework checks
make ci                               # the full Rust workspace gate (cargo make ci)
```

The framework checks are plain cargo tests at `tests/framework_quality/` — only a Rust toolchain is required. They run inside `cargo make ci` with the rest of the workspace suite.

For generated crates in downstream consumer projects, the normal verification commands apply:

```bash
cd crates/<name> && cargo check
cd crates/<name> && cargo test
cargo build --target wasm32-wasip2 --release
cargo fmt -- --check
cargo clippy -- -D warnings
```

## Code Style And Constraints

### Microsoft Pragmatic Rust Style

- Strong typing with newtypes
- Explicit error handling
- Clear, descriptive naming
- Prefer small functions and explain genuinely complex logic

### Markdown style

- Do not hard-wrap prose in Markdown files solely for column width. Keep paragraphs and list-item prose on a single line unless the line break is semantically meaningful.
- Preserve intentional line breaks in frontmatter, tables, lists, blockquotes, and fenced code blocks.

### WASM And Omnia SDK Constraints

See [guardrails.md](https://github.com/augentic/specify-adapters/blob/main/targets/omnia/references/guardrails.md) for forbidden crates and APIs, provider trait rules, validation placement, and runtime constraints.

## File Locations

In downstream consumer projects:

- **Crates**: `$PROJECT_DIR/crates/<crate_name>/`
- **Metrics**: `$PROJECT_DIR/.metrics.json` when tracking is enabled

In this repository:

- **Working artifacts**: `$PROJECT_DIR/.specify/slices/<slice-name>/` (with per-source evidence at `evidence/<source>.yaml`)
- **Baseline specs**: `$PROJECT_DIR/.specify/specs/`
- **Plan + discovery**: `$PROJECT_DIR/{change.md,plan.yaml,discovery.md}` — operator-facing platform artifacts at the project root, alongside `registry.yaml` (workspace mode places these at the workspace root)

## Troubleshooting

### Artifact Issues

- Mark uncertain behavior with `[unknown]`; mark authority-resolved disagreements with `[divergence]`; mark unresolvable same-authority disagreements with `[conflict]`. Tags never park the slice — the lifecycle still transitions to `refined`.
- Keep specs behavioral and technical detail in `design.md`
- Review `docs/explanation/augentic-specify-usage.md` when artifact responsibilities feel blurred

### Generation Issues

- Check the relevant `SKILL.md` first
- Review Omnia references for target and provider patterns
- Compare against worked examples before inventing a new pattern

## Skill authoring conventions

Every `SKILL.md` follows the house style in [docs/standards/skill-authoring.md](../../docs/standards/skill-authoring.md). Framework checks are plain cargo tests at [`tests/framework_quality/`](../../tests/framework_quality/), with policy as constants in each test module. The authoritative JSON Schemas are embedded in the `specify` binary and consumed by the same tests. See [docs/contributing/checks.md](../../docs/contributing/checks.md) for the extension model.

## For Contributors

- All skills follow the shared `SKILL.md` structure — see [docs/standards/skill-authoring.md](../../docs/standards/skill-authoring.md) for the full rationale.
- Changes to generation behavior belong in the relevant skill or reference
- Keep the repo aligned with the Specify-first operating model

